.TH PATH_CONCATB 3
.SH NAME
path_concatb \- concatenate two path buffers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "void path_concatb(const char* " a ", size_t " alen ", const char* " b ", size_t " blen ", stralloc* " out ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_concatb
concatenates two path components,
.I a
(length
.IR alen )
and
.I b
(length
.IR blen ),
into the
.B stralloc
structure
.IR out .
.PP
The function handles path separators automatically, ensuring one is inserted between the two components if necessary. It also performs a basic cleanup by removing leading "./" sequences from the resulting path if they appear at the very start.
.PP
The resulting string in
.I out
is null-terminated.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_append (3),
.BR path_join (3),
.BR stralloc (3)